1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Action Receipt helps students review a notice
without losing the original instructions.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
This notice is invented. The local rules scan it
freshly. Nothing starts approved.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Registration and payment have separate deadlines.
Each proposal links to its exact source passage.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The rules missed the consent-form instruction.
Add the action from its supporting words.

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:02,000
A source decision does not approve the action
or give it a date. Review remains separate.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The separate membership fee is explicitly waived.
Record the reason without creating a payment task.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Check each action and any condition that applies.
Confirm only complete dates and cutoff details.

8
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:41,000
"Next Friday" stays unresolved.
The consent form has no stated deadline.

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:54,000
After review: four checklist tasks,
but only two eligible calendar entries.

10
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Preview the exact files before downloading.
Source quotes and original warnings stay attached.

11
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Nothing is sent or added to a calendar automatically.
Unclear dates stay out of the calendar.

12
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Built with Codex and the Devpost Learn Skill Pack.
Runs offline with text rules, no model or API credits.
